<title>USA: News Corp's US bonds up on Cablevision plan.</title>
<headline>News Corp's US bonds up on Cablevision plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corporate bonds of News Corp gained three to five basis points on Thursday on news that Cablevision Systems Corp was getting serious about buying a 50 percent stake in the Madison Square Garden properties, analysts said.</p>
<p>News Corp in conjunction with Liberty Media Corp, a unit of Tele-Communications Inc, was considered to be one the leading contenders to buy the stake which analysts value at around $750 million.</p>
<p>&quot;People are breathing a sigh of relief,&quot; said Stuart Rossmiller, analyst at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
</text>
